WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.307
Beginners often wonder whether they should use a function, a dictionary, or a class.

00:00:05.307 --> 00:00:09.682
A function is best when you need to perform one reusable task.

00:00:09.682 --> 00:00:15.882
For example, get_profit can receive sales and costs and return the profit.

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:20.497
A dictionary is best when you mainly need to store related values.

00:00:20.497 --> 00:00:25.752
For example, a product dictionary might store the product name and price.

00:00:25.752 --> 00:00:29.812
A class is best when data and behavior belong together.

00:00:29.812 --> 00:00:37.042
For example, a Product class might store a price and also have a method that calculates the sale

00:00:37.042 --> 00:00:38.362
price. The beginner rule is to start simple.

00:00:38.362 --> 00:00:44.047
Do not use a class just because it sounds advanced.

00:00:44.047 --> 00:00:46.752
If a function solves the problem clearly, use a function.

00:00:46.752 --> 00:00:52.792
If you only need to store related values, a dictionary may be enough.

00:00:52.792 --> 00:00:56.742
Move to a class when one concept has both stored data and repeated actions.

00:00:56.742 --> 00:01:01.822
This decision is part of writing clean code.

00:01:01.822 --> 00:01:05.107
The goal is not to use the most advanced tool.

00:01:05.107 --> 00:01:07.840
The goal is to use the right tool for the job.
